<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261015032500 +0000" stop="20261015035500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">What In the World</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Honduras</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">Timber is one of this country's biggest natural resources and the source of great potential wealth. Hence the existence of wholesale illegal logging, irrespective of the consequences to the local environment. This has led concerned parties to set up the Olancho Environmental Movement. This organization has mobilized to protect these forests, at some risk to its members, like Rene Gradiz, whose testimony is disturbing in the extreme.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire de société</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/8/9/9/15271998.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E3</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261015035500 +0000" stop="20261015042500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">What In the World</title>
    <desc lang="fr">Presented by Peadar King, this series illustrates the human consequences of global economic inequalities and human rights violations, by focusing on how people encounter these issues on a daily basis.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire de société</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/8/9/9/15271998.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">E4</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261015042500 +0000" stop="20261015051000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Past Hunters</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">The Haunted Mill - Part 2</sub-title>
