    <title>Grønland</title>
    <sub-title>In the Glare of Ice</sub-title>
    <desc>Greenland is the largest island in the world and the landmass closest to the North Pole.  80% of the country is covered by a layer of ice up to 3000 meters thick. Most of the inhabitants of the country are spread over the breathtaking landscape of the ice-free west coast. The country is mostly inhabited by Inuit, who have been feeding on what nature has provided them for thousands of years. But the original life is in a state of change. The modernisation of society and man-made global warming threaten the Arctic natural paradise that is so incredibly important for our planet. Through the eyes of locals we get to know the authentic Greenland</desc>
    <icon src="https://tvpnlogopeu.samsungcloud.tv/platform/image/contents/vc/00/LINEAR/GB_USQU352137A_1384399441_0_20251127T214509869Z_33_imageprocessorclient-tvplus-linear-85d7d49859-drfrv.jpeg" />
